# **An IMS record nobody accepted or rejected** — Plan 123 Slice H.
#
# Under the Invoice Management System a record the recipient leaves alone
# before the cut-off is **deemed accepted**, and its credit flows into GSTR-2B
# on that basis. Silence is therefore a decision, and it is the only one in
# the system whose consequence arrives by default — nobody makes it
# deliberately, which is precisely why it needs a rule.
#
# **`imsStatus` absent is not the same as pending, and this rule reports
# only the explicit pending state.** A deployment that never ingested IMS
# data at all would otherwise have every invoice reported as about to be
# deemed accepted — a screen full of urgent findings manufactured out of
# missing data. `requires` handles the absent case at the outcome level, where
# it belongs: not evaluated, rather than clean or alarming.

PREFIX gst: <https://graph-owl.dev/packs/gst#>

SELECT ?invoice ?number ?gstin ?taxAmount ?imsStatus
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?register {
    ?invoice a gst:PurchaseInvoice ;
             gst:issuedBy      ?supplier ;
             gst:invoiceNumber ?number ;
             gst:taxAmount     ?taxAmount ;
             gst:imsStatus     ?imsStatus .
    ?supplier gst:supplierGstin ?gstin .
  }

  FILTER (?imsStatus = "Pending" || ?imsStatus = "pending" || ?imsStatus = "No Action")
}
ORDER BY ?number
